course: dictionary
lesson: 3818
title: Forgetfulness: a noun for a habit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Forgetful means often forgetting things. The ending -ness turns it into a noun, forgetfulness, which names the quality of being forgetful. Look for -ness at the end of a word, and you may have found a noun.
explain: In everyday life, forgetfulness shows up as forgotten homework, lost keys or a PE kit left at home. «Sam's forgetfulness meant he left his PE kit at home again.» The sentence tells you that the forgetting happened more than once, because of the word again.
explain: Read the context of «the gift of forgetfulness». The book calls it «the last best gift that the kindly demi-god is careful to bestow». The words gift, kindly and bestow (give) show that, in this story, forgetfulness is something given as a good thing, not a problem.
fact: Forgetfulness means being forgetful, which is often forgetting things.
fact: «Forgetfulness» is a noun. The ending -ness turns the adjective forgetful into a noun.
fact: Forgetfulness can come with tiredness, old age or illness.
fact: In stories, a character's forgetfulness can cause funny or exciting problems.
fact: In the book, «the gift of forgetfulness» is given by a kindly demi-god. A demi-god is a half-god, and to bestow something is to give it.
exercise: What does forgetfulness mean? | Being full of ideas | Remembering every single thing you learn | Being very fast at running | *Often forgetting things
exercise: «Sam's forgetfulness meant he left his PE kit at home again.» What does forgetfulness mean here? | *Often forgetting things | Always remembering things | Being cold | Losing his football
exercise: The book says the demi-god will «bestow» the gift. What does bestow mean? | Break | *Give | Hide | Take away
test: Forgetfulness can come with which of these? | Being on time for everything | Reading a long book | *Tiredness, old age or illness | Winning a race
test: In a story, what might a character's forgetfulness cause? | Perfect homework every day | *Funny or exciting problems | A quiet, boring day with nothing to do | Nothing at all, ever
exam: What is a demi-god? | A king with a golden crown | *A half-god | A bird that can talk | A full god who rules the sky
